ame\":\"\",\"type\":\"address\",\"internalType\":\"contract SimpleMintableERC20\"}],\"stateMutability\":\"view\"}],\"devdoc\":{\"kind\":\"dev\",\"methods\":{\"hasPartialCase()\":{\"details\":\"False: a Uni V2 pair has no capacity gate, so `limitCapacity` cannot be honoured and the\"},\"limitCapacity(uint256)\":{\"details\":\"Records intent only; AMM capacity is not gated.\"},\"armOperativeRevert()\":{\"details\":\"Zap-in ends in `router.addLiquidity` -> `pair.mint(address)`; rejecting the pair's mint\"}},\"details\":\"Idempotence: the package is CREATE3-deployed under a release salt and binds the factory and\\n *      router as immutables with no getters. A later fixture of the same test therefore passes the\\n *      previous fixture as `existingFixture` and reuses its `pkg()`, `factory()` and `router()`;\\n *      only the tokens, the pair and the SE are new. `address(0)` deploys everything.R14 / D33: Uni V2 has no protocol capacity gate, so `limitCapacity` only records intent and\\n *      `hasPartialCase()` is false (the row runs the rounding-to-zero control). The AMM leftover\\n *      case is covered by `seBooked()` (the SE's reserved face leftover, `reserveOfToken(face)`)\\n *      and `test_row_ammCallerFundSeparation`: booked leftover is never refunded or paired with a\\n *      later caller's other token.\\n \",\"errors\":{\"DependencyRejected(bytes32)\":[{\"details\":\"Non-SUT dependency failure payload used by `armOperativeRevert` implementations.\"}]},\"stateVariables\":{\"deployer\":{\"details\":\"The test contract that created this fixture; it owns `create3Factory` (CraneTest `initEnv`).\"},\"capacityIntent\":{\"details\":\"Recorded `limitCapacity` intent; AMMs cannot honour it (see contract NatSpec).\"}},\"title\":\"SeMatrix_UniV2Fixture\",\"version\":1},\"userdoc\":{\"kind\":\"user\",\"methods\":{\"pkg()\":{\"notice\":\"Package deployed by the first fixture of a test; later fixtures reuse it.\"},\"seedLiquidity(uint256)\":{\"notice\":\"Add `amountEa